{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210733,"nonce":"xsOSrqKYScI7xGuP/jtwarZEkbw=","title":"AOT GC Pass-1 walker marked fp covered before metadata lookup","message":"Fixed in commit d8739d9. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n`scan_native_stack_roots` runs in two passes. Pass 1 reads the global `jit_frame_entries` list (the `(fp, func_id, ret_addr)` triples pushed by `wren_call_N` wrappers); Pass 2 walks the native FP chain for any AOT frame that didn't get a push.\n\nThe original Pass 1 inserted `jit_fp` into `covered_fps` **before** the `jit_metadata.get(func_id).and_then(|m| m.as_ref())` lookup. When that lookup returns None, Pass 1 hits the `continue` and the frame is never scanned — but `covered_fps` still has it. Pass 2 then walks the chain, finds a frame whose `saved_fp` matches the covered entry, and skips that too. Net result: the AOT body's spill slots aren't visible to the GC at all.\n\nThe wrong-func_id case is real: AOT registration calls `register_aot_function(name_sym = \"\u003caot-frame\u003e\", ...)` which synthesises a fresh FuncId for code-range bookkeeping, but `call_constructor_sync_impl` sets `JitContext.current_func_id` to the MIR FuncId and `wren_call_0_inner` reads that to push the frame. So Pass 1's lookup is against the MIR FuncId while AOT metadata sits under the AOT FuncId — guaranteed miss.\n\nWhy: the receiver's nursery address is pinned in `ss0` across the toString call (constructor → `wren_call_0` → `wren_call_0_inner` → dispatch → toString impl → finish_alloc → GC). When the GC misses the frame, the receiver gets promoted to old-gen but ss0 is never written back. The next nursery reset reuses the same nursery byte range for the concat-result string, and the constructor's second field store reads ss0 (now a String pointer), dereferences `*(string_header + 32)` expecting the Instance's fields ptr, and crashes.\n\nHow to apply: when adding new pass-1 entries or new code paths that push jit frames, make sure `covered_fps` only records frames we *actually* scanned. The fix is a one-line move of `covered_fps.insert(jit_fp)` to immediately before the `for root in roots_to_scan { … }` loop, after every \"we have metadata AND a matching safepoint\" check has passed.\n\nRepro: `tests/aot_gc_coverage.rs::stress_mixed_alloc_chain` — was `#[ignore]`'d, now passes.\n\nRelated: [[project-aot-gc-stack-map-gap]] (parent investigation), [[project-jit-root-arg-pattern]] (the JIT-root push convention that the AOT path inherits).","files":null}]}